    "problem_statement": "QR code generation fails with IndexError: list index out of range\n\n#### Description\n\nWhen trying to generate QR codes, the library crashes with an IndexError during the format information setup process. This affects all QR code generation functionality.\n\n#### Steps/Code to Reproduce\n\n```python\nimport qrcode\n\n# Basic QR code generation\nqr = qrcode.QRCode()\nqr.add_data('Hello World')\nqr.make()\n\n# This will raise IndexError: list index out of range\nimg = qr.make_image()\n```\n\nThe error occurs during the internal format information processing when the QR code matrix is being constructed. Any attempt to generate a QR code, regardless of the data or settings, results in the same IndexError.\n\n#### Expected Behavior\n\nQR codes should generate successfully without throwing IndexError exceptions.\n\n#### Environment\n\n- Python version: 3.10.15\n- qrcode library version: latest"
